# Hackathon Management System Implementation Plan

Transforming HackOS into a production-ready Hackathon Management System for Fraylon Technologies.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Google Form Integration**: Initial team registration will be handled via Google Forms/Sheets. I will implement the Firebase side to receive/ingest this data or provide instructions for manual import/Apps Script setup.
> - **Role Sync**: Roles will be stored in Firestore `users` document. Admin/Judge roles must be set manually in Firestore initially or via a special UI.

## Proposed Changes

### [Core Refactor]
Refactor `src` structure to separate logic by role and responsibility.

#### [MODIFY] [App.jsx](file:///d:/Visual%20Studio%20Code/Projects/hackathon/HackOS/src/App.jsx)
- Update routing to include Admin and Judge dashboards.
- Wrap routes in `ProtectedRoute` with role requirements.

#### [NEW] [folder structure](file:///d:/Visual%20Studio%20Code/Projects/hackathon/HackOS/src/)
- `src/services/`: Firebase interaction logic.
- `src/hooks/`: Data fetching and role checks.
- `src/layouts/`: Role-specific dashboard layouts.
- `src/components/admin/`: Admin-specific components.
- `src/components/judge/`: Judge-specific components.
- `src/components/participant/`: Participant-specific components.

### [Firestore Schema]

#### `users`
```json
{
  "uid": "string",
  "name": "string",
  "email": "string",
  "role": "admin | judge | participant",
  "teamId": "string (optional)"
}
```

#### `teams`
```json
{
  "teamId": "string",
  "teamName": "string",
  "leaderEmail": "string",
  "members": ["string"],
  "college": "string",
  "paymentStatus": "pending | verified | rejected",
  "paymentScreenshot": "url",
  "round1Status": "qualified | rejected | pending",
  "round2Status": "qualified | rejected | pending",
  "totalScore": 0,
  "createdAt": "timestamp"
}
```

#### `submissions`
```json
{
  "teamId": "string",
  "pptLink": "string",
  "githubLink": "string",
  "deployLink": "string",
  "submittedAt": "timestamp"
}
```

### [Security Rules]
Implement production-ready Firestore rules to protect data based on user roles and team ownership.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- CLI validation of Firestore rules.
- Manual verification of GitHub repo existence via `fetch`.

### Manual Verification
- Test login with different roles.
- Verify that a participant cannot access the Admin dashboard.
- Verify that scores auto-calculate and update the leaderboard.
